Z||000003||MikeSchaefer||03-18-2001||06:27 PM||||Why are there so many rumors about cars having suspensions developed by Lotus?  I've talked to a thousand different car owners claiming this (even crx and mr2 owners)? also I realize that lotus makes beautiful cars, but are they even the king of suspensions anyways?  I have always assumed they are, but I have never really questioned it.  I think it is high time this urban legend was killed, before the days of the internet's vast wisdom these rumors would have been more believable I guess.  I drive a Delorean (the real deal Lotus connection, and it isn't even par with my 84's handling (or speed or finish)<BR>Kinda weird I think||||reg||4
Z||000004||Slammed Fiero||03-18-2001||06:56 PM||||Lotus did have a lot of influence in designing the Toyota MR2's suspension..the Mk1 , not sure about the other years. I have seen this on several Mr2 sites as well first hand from Mr2 friends.<P>JM||||reg||1
Z||000005||88formula||03-18-2001||07:34 PM||||What makes Lotus engineers any better than the other company engineers? I think the budget of the company making the car has more influence on the suspension used than who designed it. Lotus is just a name!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
